  "scope": "Native managed account-root cleanup ownership, historical recovery and successor lifetime. No installed foreign root-lifecycle or full release claim.",
  "behavior": [
    "One private Original variant owns preparing enrollment, fenced root recovery or retired enrollment; each successful cleanup step retains the same registry.",
    "Native historical cleanup remains bound to the original paths, intent, witness and committed proposal/checkpoint. Successful old-signer erasure reopens only that original historical parent.",
    "Ordinary preparation, alternate-target and committed-winner adoption resume after journal/signer erasure. Retries preserve revision 2, old-root fencing and independent current successor admission.",
    "Preparing/Pending refuse the callback. Missing originals are not recreated. Callback/storage errors close the controller and revoke cached successor access.",
    "Operation scope owns the controller until success. Callback unwind drops it and revokes delegated owners while propagating the original panic.",
    "Expired successor credentials still refuse activation; independently authorized historical accounting/erasure remains available."
